# 7.3.acuity.envelope.watch.stone

## .what

set the **watchful-wait tier** — which live scenarios are benign enough to observe at home, the
observation cadence, and the **tripwires** that escalate a watched case to same-day or emergency. this
is the floor band of the acuity envelope, and it closes the envelope with an explicit safety net.

## .inputs

- `7.1.acuity.envelope.emergency.yield.md` — the emergency floor
- `7.2.acuity.envelope.sameday.yield.md` — the same-day tier
- `6.1.scenario.superposition.bounds.yield.md` — the best-case bounds

## .do

- for the live scenarios whose worst-case bound is benign / self-limited, state the **watch** plan:
  what to observe and how often
- write the **tripwires** — the concrete observations that promote a watched case up the envelope
  (to same-day per 7.2, or emergency per 7.1)
- state plainly: watchful wait is only licensed while every catastrophic branch stays eliminated or
  is covered by a tripwire (`rule.require.superposition-until-elimination`)

## .emit

into `7.3.acuity.envelope.watch.yield.md` — the watch tier, the observation cadence, and the
tripwires that escalate.

## .done when

the watch tier is stated with its cadence, the tripwires are listed, and the envelope is closed —
every live scenario sits in exactly one acuity band.
